  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 114 AM CDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, some rain has moved into north central and \ncentral SD. This is expected to spread east and continue through the \nday today. Some weak thunderstorms are also possible with no severe \nstorms expected. Temperatures across the region are in the mid 50s \nwith light winds. Some fog will be possible around and east of I-29 \nthis morning.\n\nAs mentioned, rain and some thunderstorms are expected to continue \nthrough the day and into Tuesday, with some chances lingering \nthrough Wednesday afternoon over far eastern SD into west central \nMN. While the amounts expected haven't changed too much, the spacial \nextent of those amounts has. The 50-70% chance of more than a half \ninch of rain between this morning and Tuesday morning now extends as \nfar south as Pierre and as far east as Aberdeen and Redfield. This \nis a pretty decent southward expansion compared to 24 hours ago. \nThis is a result of a slight change in the track of the low. With \nthe precipitation expected to last into Wednesday afternoon over \neastern SD and west central MN, the chance of half inch is around 50-\n70%, generally east of the Prairie Coteau. The rest of the forecast \nlooks to be a lot drier.\n\nTemperatures are still expected to be right around to slightly above \naverage through the middle of the week and turn towards slightly \nbelow average for the second half of the week into the weekend. \nWinds across central SD will start to gust 25 to 30 mph this \nmorning, with gusts of 35 mph possible across south central SD \nthrough the late evening. Gusts of 25 to 30 mph will spread east to \naround the James River this afternoon and continue into the evening. \nWinds Friday may gust up to 30 mph west of the Missouri River.",
